flowchart TB
    accTitle: Join the lobby with a parked player
    accDescr: Ada plays on the page and opens a lobby on Autodarts at the board of the display. On that page, the tile of each parked player in the popup and in the switcher offers Join the lobby. A tap on Bob's renews his parked session and keeps the rotated token first. When his session is dead or Autodarts can't be reached, his tile says why and nothing else changes. Otherwise the extension seats Bob at the board of the display with his own access token, which never reaches the page. When Autodarts refuses the seat because the lobby is full, closed or started, the popup says so. Otherwise his tile says In the lobby, the page stays with Ada without a switch or a reload, and the match counts for both accounts.

    lobby["Ada plays on the page<br>and opens a lobby at the board of the display"]
    tiles["The popup and the switcher:<br>Join the lobby on each parked player's tile"]
    tap["A tap on Join the lobby<br>below Bob's tile"]
    renew{"Renew Bob's parked session<br>and keep the rotated token"}
    why["Bob's tile says why:<br>sign in again, or try again later"]
    seat{"Seat Bob at the board of the display,<br>with his own access token"}
    refused["The popup says so:<br>the lobby is full, closed or started"]
    seated["Bob's tile says In the lobby;<br>the page stays with Ada, no switch, no reload"]
    stats["The match counts for Ada and for Bob"]

    lobby --> tiles --> tap --> renew
    renew -- "dead or unreachable" --> why
    renew -- "fresh" --> seat
    seat -- "refused" --> refused
    seat -- "seated" --> seated --> stats

    classDef bot fill:#526cfe2e,stroke:#526cfe,stroke-width:2px
    classDef person fill:#f59e0b2e,stroke:#f59e0b,stroke-width:2px
    classDef done fill:#16a34a2e,stroke:#16a34a,stroke-width:2px
    class tiles,renew,seat bot
    class lobby,tap person
    class seated,stats done
